<title>ABU DHABI: UAE's Etisalat 1996 net rises to 1.7 bln dirhams.</title>
<headline>UAE's Etisalat 1996 net rises to 1.7 bln dirhams.</headline>
<dateline>ABU DHABI 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>	  (in billions of dirhams)</p>
<p> Net profit		1.70	 1.45</p>
<p> Operating profit	1.50	 1.27</p>
<p> Turnover		  3.78	 3.21</p>
<p> Shareholder's Funds   5.12	 4.35</p>
<p>Full name: Emirates Telecommunications Corp</p>
<p>Note: The company said turnover growth was largely due to volume growth in international traffic generated from fixed telephones as well as cellular GSM telephones.</p>
<p>Etisalat's board of directors in January announced a 50 dirham dividend to be paid in two installments of 25 dirhams each. The board also approved a one-for-four bonus share issue.</p>
<p>The UAE government owns 60 percent of Etisalat. ($1=3.67 dirhams) -- Dubai newsroom +9714 6071 222</p>
